  "id": "taste-aversion-learning",
  "term": "taste-aversion learning",
  "definition": "Taste-aversion learning is a form of learning in which an animal comes to avoid a taste after that taste has been associated with an unpleasant bodily consequence such as illness. In this packet, it is discussed as conditioned taste aversion and as involving learning and memory related to the gustatory cortex.",
